# Security rules

## Doc map

- **Setup & commands** → [README.md](../../README.md)
- **System design & deployment** → [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md)
- **Stack, paths & conventions** → [PROJECT.md](../../PROJECT.md)

## Secrets & logging

- Never commit secrets, tokens, or credentials to source.
- Do not log PII, session tokens, or other sensitive values.

## Untrusted content

- Avoid `innerHTML`, `eval`, `new Function`, and dynamic script injection.
- Validate and encode untrusted values before putting them into URLs, HTML attributes, or external requests.

## Network boundaries

- Keep network access in typed wrappers or clearly isolated modules, not scattered through UI code.
- Validate external API responses before trusting their shape.
- Do not use `mode: "no-cors"` to hide CORS problems.

## Dependencies & legal copy

- Prefer maintained dependencies and address high-severity audit findings before release.
- Ask before editing legal or privacy copy.
